# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SendGrid Azure Group Management (Planning Scaffold)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Purpose
# - Move SendGrid access management to Entra ID (Azure AD) group-driven sync.
# - This script will eventually read group membership from Graph and enforce
#   matching teammate/subuser access in SendGrid.
#
# Current state
# - Planning/comments only. No operational code yet.
#
# Core model
# - Source of truth: Entra groups.
# - Target system: SendGrid teammates + subuser persona scopes.
# - Sync strategy: idempotent reconciliation (desired state vs actual state).
#
# Access categories
# 1) Account Admin
#    - Access to everything and all subusers.
#    - Group: cs-sendgrid-admin
#
# 2) Account Read-Only
#    - Read-only on main account and all subusers.
#    - Group: cs-sendgrid-admin-ro
#
# 3) Subuser Persona Access
#    - Scoped access per subuser and per persona.
#    - Group format: cs-sendgrid-$Subuser-$Persona
#    - Persona scopes reference:
#      https://www.twilio.com/docs/sendgrid/ui/account-and-settings/teammate-permissions#persona-scopes
#
# Proposed naming conventions
# - Normalize subuser token from SendGrid username (or canonical key).
# - Normalize persona token to a stable slug (lowercase, hyphen-safe).
# - Final group key is case-insensitive for matching.
#
# Examples
# - cs-sendgrid-admin
# - cs-sendgrid-admin-ro
# - cs-sendgrid-marketing-prod-analyst
# - cs-sendgrid-support-emea-developer
#
# High-level sync flow (future implementation)
# 1) Bootstrap/auth
#    - Resolve ScriptDir, load local variables and shared auth helpers.
#    - Connect to Graph (app-only cert auth pattern in this repo).
#    - Connect to SendGrid via shared SendGrid API function wrappers.
#
# 2) Discover desired state from Graph
#    - Query members of:
#      - cs-sendgrid-admin
#      - cs-sendgrid-admin-ro
#      - all cs-sendgrid-<subuser>-<persona> groups
#    - Expand users to canonical identity key (UPN only).
#
# 3) Discover current state from SendGrid
#    - Enumerate teammates on the parent account for account-level admin/admin-ro.
#    - Enumerate teammates in each subuser context via on-behalf-of for subuser personas.
#
# 4) Build reconciliation model
#    - Desired assignments by user:
#      - account role: admin | admin-ro | none
#      - subuser persona list: [{ subuser, persona }...]
#    - Current assignments by user from SendGrid.
#
# 5) Reconcile changes (idempotent)
#    - Create SSO teammates directly in the target subuser context (on-behalf-of).
#    - Update teammate role/persona scopes in that same subuser context.
#    - Remove stale scopes.
#    - Optional: deactivate/remove teammate when no assignments remain.
#
# 6) Reporting
#    - Summarize adds/updates/removals/no-change.
#    - Emit warnings for unknown groups/personas/subusers.
#    - Dry-run mode should print proposed actions only.
#
# Conflict handling rules (proposed)
# - If user is in both admin and admin-ro groups, admin wins.
# - If user has admin, subuser persona group assignments are redundant and
#   should be ignored (or logged as informational) unless business rules say
#   otherwise.
# - If group references unknown subuser/persona, do not fail whole run;
#   record warning and continue.
#
# Identity and matching rules (proposed)
# - Primary user key: UPN (lowercase, trimmed).
# - Secondary fallback: mail.
# - Avoid display-name matching.
# - Keep a deterministic map between Entra user and SendGrid teammate identity.
#
# Guardrails and safety (future requirements)
# - Support -WhatIf / dry-run first-class behavior.
# - Explicit confirmation for destructive removals outside dry-run.
# - Optional allowlist for target groups.
# - Optional denylist for protected teammates.
# - Retry/backoff for Graph and SendGrid transient API failures.
#
# Operational concerns
# - Respect SendGrid and Graph API throttling.
# - Batch/paginate reads where possible.
# - Keep secret material in memory only.
# - Do not write API keys or sensitive payloads to logs.
#
# Open design questions to finalize before coding
# - Exact mapping table for each persona slug -> SendGrid persona scope payload.
# - Whether "admin-ro" should map to SendGrid built-in role or custom scopes.
# - Whether orphaned teammates should be removed or only disabled.
# - Required exception process for one-off manual access.
# - Notification channel for reconciliation changes/failures.
#
# Suggested implementation phases
# Phase 1: Read-only inventory and diff report.
# Phase 2: Create/update teammate role and subuser persona assignments.
# Phase 3: Safe cleanup/removal workflow with approvals.
# Phase 4: Scheduled automation + monitoring/alerting.
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------

